@startuml
title Smart Apartment System - Amenities Module (3/3: BOOKING MANAGEMENT)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam dpi 75

actor Admin as A
actor Resident as R
participant "Client App" as App
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Amenities API" as API
database "Database" as DB

note over A, Gateway: Admin requests include: Authorization: Bearer {admin_token}
note over R, Gateway: Resident requests include: Authorization: Bearer {resident_token}

== RESIDENT: BOOK A SLOT ==

R -> App: Book slot
App -> Gateway: POST /bookings {slotId, peopleCount: 2}
Gateway -> API: Forward booking request

API -> DB: Begin transaction\nLock slot row for update
DB --> API: {slotType, maxCapacity, slotDate}

alt slotDate < CURRENT_DATE
    API -> DB: Rollback
    API --> Gateway: 422 Unprocessable Entity\n"Cannot book past slot"
    Gateway --> App: Error
    App --> R: "Cannot book a past slot"

else slotType == 'TIME'
    API -> DB: Check if slot already has an active booking
    DB --> API: bookingCount

    alt bookingCount == 0
        API -> API: Force peopleCount = 1
        API -> DB: Insert booking record\nUpdate slot current bookings to 1\nCommit transaction
        DB --> API: booking_id
        API --> Gateway: 201 Created {bookingId}
        Gateway --> App: Booking confirmed
        App --> R: "Booking successful! ID: {bookingId}"
    else bookingCount > 0
        API -> DB: Rollback
        API --> Gateway: 409 Conflict - Slot already booked
        Gateway --> App: Error
        App --> R: "Slot already booked"
    end

else slotType == 'TIME_COUNT'
    API -> DB: Fetch total people already booked in this slot
    DB --> API: totalPeople

    alt totalPeople + peopleCount <= maxCapacity
        API -> DB: Insert booking record\nIncrement slot current bookings by peopleCount\nCommit transaction
        DB --> API: booking_id
        API --> Gateway: 201 Created {bookingId}
        Gateway --> App: Booking confirmed
        App --> R: "Booking successful! ID: {bookingId}"
    else totalPeople + peopleCount > maxCapacity
        API -> DB: Rollback
        API --> Gateway: 409 Conflict - Not enough capacity
        Gateway --> App: Error
        App --> R: "Not enough capacity available"
    end
end

== RESIDENT: VIEW BOOKING HISTORY ==

R -> App: View my bookings
App -> Gateway: GET /bookings\n?status=BOOKED&fromDate=2024-07-01&toDate=2024-07-31\n&pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Gateway -> API: Forward with user context
API -> DB: Fetch bookings for current user filtered by status and date range
DB --> API: Bookings list with amenity and slot details
API --> Gateway: 200 OK {data, pagination}
Gateway --> App: Display booking history
App --> R: "Showing 2 active bookings"

R -> App: Filter bookings by CANCELLED status
App -> Gateway: GET /bookings?status=CANCELLED&pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Gateway -> API: Forward request
API -> DB: Fetch cancelled bookings for current user
DB --> API: Cancelled bookings list
API --> Gateway: 200 OK {data, pagination}
Gateway --> App: Display cancelled bookings
App --> R: "Showing 1 cancelled booking"

== RESIDENT: CANCEL BOOKING ==

R -> App: Cancel booking
App -> Gateway: DELETE /bookings/{bookingId}
Gateway -> API: Forward cancellation

API -> DB: Begin transaction\nLock booking row for update
DB --> API: {status, slotDate, slotType, peopleCount}

alt status == 'CANCELLED'
    API -> DB: Rollback
    API --> Gateway: 400 Bad Request - Booking already cancelled
    Gateway --> App: Error
    App --> R: "Booking already cancelled"

else slotDate < CURRENT_DATE
    API -> DB: Rollback
    API --> Gateway: 400 Bad Request - Cannot cancel past booking
    Gateway --> App: Error
    App --> R: "Cannot cancel past booking"

else status == 'BOOKED'
    API -> DB: Update booking status to CANCELLED
    DB --> API: Updated

    alt slotType == 'TIME_COUNT'
        API -> DB: Decrease slot current bookings by peopleCount
        DB --> API: Updated
        note right: Released {peopleCount} spots back to pool
    else slotType == 'TIME'
        API -> DB: Reset slot current bookings to 0
        DB --> API: Updated
        note right: Released the single spot back
    end

    API -> DB: Commit botransaction
    API --> Gateway: 200 OK {message: "Booking cancelled successfully"}
    Gateway --> App: Cancellation confirmed
    App --> R: "Booking cancelled. Spots released."
end

== CONCURRENT BOOKING SCENARIO (TIME_COUNT SLOT) ==

note over R: Two residents booking the same TIME_COUNT slot simultaneously

R -> App: Resident A books 3 people
App -> Gateway: POST /bookings {slotId: "gym-slot", peopleCount: 3}
Gateway -> API: Forward Booking A

API -> DB: Begin transaction - Lock slot row
DB --> API: {maxCapacity: 10, currentBookings: 2}
note right: Lock acquired by Booking A

R -> App: Resident B books 4 people at the same time
App -> Gateway: POST /bookings {slotId: "gym-slot", peopleCount: 4}
Gateway -> API: Forward Booking B
API -> DB: Attempt to lock same slot row
note right: Booking B waits - lock held by A

API -> API: Validate: 2 + 3 = 5 is within capacity 10
API -> DB: Insert Booking A\nUpdate currentBookings to 5\nCommit - lock released
DB --> API: Success
API --> Gateway: 201 Created - Booking A success
Gateway --> App: Booking A confirmed
App --> R: "Booking A successful"

API -> DB: Lock acquired by Booking B\nReads updated currentBookings = 5
API -> API: Validate: 5 + 4 = 9 is within capacity 10
API -> DB: Insert Booking B\nUpdate currentBookings to 9\nCommit transaction
DB --> API: Success
API --> Gateway: 201 Created - Booking B success
Gateway --> App: Booking B confirmed
App --> R: "Booking B successful"
note over R: Both succeeded - total (9) is within capacity (10)

== BOOKING FAILURE - CAPACITY EXCEEDED ==

R -> App: Book when capacity is nearly full
App -> Gateway: POST /bookings {slotId: "full-slot", peopleCount: 3}
Gateway -> API: Forward request

API -> DB: Begin transaction - Lock slot row
DB --> API: {maxCapacity: 10, currentBookings: 9}
API -> API: Validate: 9 + 3 = 12 exceeds capacity 10

API -> DB: Rollback
API --> Gateway: 409 Conflict\n"Not enough capacity (only 1 spot left)"
Gateway --> App: Error
App --> R: "Sorry, only 1 spot remaining"

== ADMIN: BOOKING REPORT ==

A -> App: Generate booking report
App -> Gateway: GET /reports/bookings
Gateway -> API: Forward request

API -> DB: Fetch booking statistics
DB --> API: Report data

API -> API: Calculate utilization

API --> Gateway: 200 OK {report}
Gateway --> App: Display report
App --> A: "150 bookings, 68.5% utilization"

@enduml
